+### Requirement: Results grid headers share one label style
+
+On the run Extraction Result grid and the Compare Execution Results grid, every header label — column
+labels and group labels alike — SHALL render in the same size, weight, sentence case and letter
+spacing (the ellipsis header components), never in the grid kit's default uppercase header text. A
+label over a column of numbers or scores (execution index, total, `HTTP`, `Duration`, metric score,
+`Delta`) SHALL sit at the right edge of its column; every other label sits at the left.
+
+#### Scenario: Default-styled columns use the shared label
+
+- **WHEN** the grid shows `Test Case name`, `Total turns`, `HTTP`, `Duration`, or a compare `Delta` column
+- **THEN** its label has the same size, weight and letter case as the metric and extracted labels
+
+#### Scenario: A metric column with a missing first value is still right-aligned
+
+- **WHEN** a metric's first result has no value but a later one does
+- **THEN** the metric's header label sits at the right edge, over its right-aligned values
+
